That's interesting. Your code makes perfect sense, but I'm not sure if passing the result from one nimbleRcall to another will be compiled correctly.  (The nimbleRcall is somewhat rudimentary.). Can you please try it if you just make a single function Rlength_unique and have a nimbleRcall to that, i.e.
Ke <- Rlength_unique(groupe[1:N])
Also I think the return type from Rlength or Rlength_unique should be double(0), indicating a scalar.
Does that work?
-Perry

