Oh, here is something I missed earlier in your code: The extent of a for loop in a model can't depend on a model variable.  You have for(j in 1:Ke), but Ke is a model variable. The reason is that the graphical structure of the model can only depend on constants.  Do the BNP examples on our examples <https://r-nimble.org/examples> page and blog <https://r-nimble.org/recent-posts> posts help?

