Hi Perry,

I get your idea. I managed to implement this model using the stick-breaking process in nimble. However, another model in my study is based on a modified Chinese restaurant process. This is why I tried to first implement the CRP-based one.

If the purpose is just for clustering, I can compute the number of clusters after obtaining the MCMC samples. But the model contains other parameters that are associated with the mixture distribution. So I think I have to incorporate the whole process into the model code.

Your suggestion is definitely enlightening to me. I will try to circumvent the issue.

Best,
Chris

